# Interpretability artefacts (protocol section 22, added at the v6 revision).
# The whole directory is pixel data or per-image arrays: 32 attribution panels are
# real de-identified knee radiographs, regions_overlay.png is a single patient's crop,
# and mean_frontal_crop.npy is a cohort mean image. src/interpretability.py regenerates
# every one of them from the shards, so none is needed for code reproducibility.
outputs/interpretability/

# Per-patient rows produced by the same module. The aggregate interp_ tables
# (summary, regions, occlusion, view_ablation, attention_*, sanity_checks,
# risk_provenance) carry no identifiers and ARE committed; these four do.
outputs/tables/interp_attribution_per_image.csv
outputs/tables/interp_attribution_registered.csv
outputs/tables/interp_attribution_sample.csv
outputs/tables/interp_panel_manifest.csv

